# ScriptedController.ChooseTargets (control.go) never validates its queued
# answer against the candidates it was offered, unlike a real player's UI or
# the AI -- this scenario uses that to isolate the CR 608.2b re-check
# (targetStillLegal -> cardCantBeTargetedBy) on its own, a target Java could
# never actually have chosen. TestTargetCandidates* (staticability_internal_test.go)
# holds the choice-time filter (targetCandidates) to the same rule directly.
# CR 702.19a: Shroud carries no Activator$ gate at all in Java
# (CardFactoryUtil.java's own Shroud branch) -- it refuses every spell or
# ability, its own controller's included. human's own Lightning Bolt at
# human's own Kalonian Behemoth is still a legal candidate when cast (the
# players remain legal candidates for ValidTgts$ Any), but the CR 608.2b
# re-check at resolution (targetStillLegal -> cardCantBeTargetedBy) finds
# the Behemoth illegal and drops it -- Bolt fizzles, dealing no damage.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 2 R
queue targets 1
queue action human cast 3
passpriority
